# Kitchen hot and cold packs: dissolving can warm or cool
#
# Equal water portions receive equal salt masses. The thermometer decides;
# "dissolving releases heat" is not a general rule. These are simulation
# samples, not food or medical-pack instructions.
register lv1

# Calcium chloride dissolution is exothermic.
add v1 water 100mL
measure v1 thermometer
add v1 CaCl2 20g
measure v1 thermometer
inspect v1

# Ammonium chloride dissolution is endothermic under the same starting
# conditions. Do not ingest laboratory ammonium salts.
new beaker
add v2 water 100mL
measure v2 thermometer
add v2 NH4Cl 20g
measure v2 thermometer
inspect v2

# Ordinary salt provides a household-scale comparison rather than another
# universal rule.
new beaker
add v3 water 100mL
measure v3 thermometer
add v3 NaCl 20g
measure v3 thermometer
inspect v3

# The vessels are adiabatic approximations. A real cup, packet and room absorb
# heat, and dissolution rate and packet construction are outside this result.

